asset:        filmagic-export.png
title:        README gallery: Export mode
author:       Filmagic contributors (screenshot); film/footage/music credits below
source:       original work (screenshot of Filmagic captured with its ui.screenshot control command)
license:      MIT OR Apache-2.0 (screenshot); embedded film frames are public domain
license-file:
added:        2026-11-12 by @vansyson1308
notes:        Export mode at 1600x1000 points (1.5x, 2400x1500 px) for the Trailer sequence: Media File destination and an empty Queue on the left; file name, a neutral example location (/media/exports), the Match Source - Adaptive High Bitrate preset, H.264 Video and AAC Audio settings in the middle; the preview on a Night of the Living Dead (1968) frame (Johnny in the cemetery), Range, Scaling and the Summary on the right. All UI icons are drawn in code; fonts are Inter and JetBrains Mono (OFL-1.1). Contains no Adobe artwork. Rebuild and recapture with the scripts in docs/images/scripts/ (README there): build_trailer.py, then capture_gallery.py export.
Media visible or used in the screenshot (none of it is committed to the repository):
  - Night of the Living Dead (1968), dir. George A. Romero, Image Ten. US public domain (released without a copyright notice). Source: https://archive.org/details/night-of-the-living-dead-1968-english (Public Domain Mark).
